n><fn id="tbfnote4"><label>b</label><p>Test for homogeneity of risk ratios among dose groups or test for trend of linear dose response; baseline rates adjusted for city, sex, year of birth, residency, and age at entry.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap> and <xref rid="tbl4" ref-type="table">4</xref> <table-wrap id="tbl4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Adjusted risk ratio for hematopoietic tumor before and after 20 years of age in the offspring, according to parental preconception exposure to radiation</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="4" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Age 1&#x02013;19 years</bold><hr/></th><th colspan="4" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Age 20&#x0002b; years</bold><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Dose (mSv)</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of cases<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Risk ratio</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>95&#x00025; CI</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic>-value<sup>b</sup></bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of cases<sup>a</sup></bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Risk ratio</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>95&#x00025; CI</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic>-value<sup>b</sup></bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>Paternal exposure</italic></td><td align="left" valign="top" char